## 2. Demo network

The default demo topology is based on the supplied C1-C6 network.

```text
                   C2
                   |
                   |
         C5 ------ C1 ------ C4
                   |
                   |
                   C3
                   |
                   |
                   C6
```

### 2.1 Node model

All nodes are configurable. For the first build:

- **C1**: primary signalized junction and main decision point.
- **C3**: secondary signalized junction / upstream feeder to C1.
- **C2, C4, C5, C6**: feeder/boundary/camera nodes. They may be modeled as signalized nodes later without changing the data model.

The system must not hard-code this topology inside UI components. Store the network as graph data so another corridor can be loaded later.

### 2.2 Primary traffic paths

- C6 -> C3 -> C1 -> C2
- C5 -> C1 -> C4
- C4 -> C1 -> C5
- C2 -> C1 -> C3 -> C6

Turning ratios are synthetic configuration for the MVP.

