## 10. Python intelligence/simulation services

### 10.1 Simulation service

Retain Python/SUMO/TraCI, seeded demand, aggregate 1 Hz stream, virtual phase progression, reset and safe plan application behind the owning Go domain service. Validate run/config identity and canonical mode contracts. Preserve deterministic seeds and clearance intervals through retries and owner changes. Actual aggregate comparison must not be described as cloned vehicle trajectories unless those trajectories are implemented and verified.

### 10.2 Intelligence service

Retain conservation forecasts, platoon propagation, bounded candidate evaluation, comparison and structured explanations behind Go. No unsupported trained-ML, confidence or performance claims. Response provenance includes run, snapshot, horizon, model/config version and recommendation identity. An unavailable worker must produce visible unavailable state, not healthy/fabricated fallback data.

The Python **gateway** is a separate responsibility from these workers. The browser must never directly address private simulation, intelligence, Go domain or writer ports.

