## 20. Recommendation explanation engine

The UI must never display only a number. Every recommendation must contain a machine-readable reason and a plain-language explanation.

Example fact payload:

```json
{
  "trigger": "spillback_risk",
  "target": "C1:northbound",
  "spillback_eta_s": 104,
  "upstream_source": "C3",
  "predicted_arrivals_120s": 36,
  "downstream_occupancy_now": 0.61,
  "downstream_occupancy_predicted": 0.94,
  "actions": [
    {"junction":"C1","phase":"NS","delta_green_s":12},
    {"junction":"C3","phase":"NB","delta_green_s":-6}
  ]
}
```

Rendered explanation:

> C1 northbound storage is predicted to exceed 90% in about 104 sec. A platoon released from C3 is expected to add approximately 36 vehicles over the next two minutes. The recommended plan increases C1 clearance while slightly reducing C3 release to prevent spillback.

Do not use an LLM to invent operational facts. If an LLM is added later, it may only verbalize structured facts produced by deterministic services.

